WEBVTT

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.720
Mm-hmm.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:21.620
I'll take the Queen

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:30.000
Now hockey while I give to you the privileges of the season there shall be no

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.840
Amusement tax on necking.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.420
Hooray!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.140
Ready!

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.180
Son of a-- you old horses.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.780
Oh, son, I'm glad to see you, you old son of a gun, you.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.480
Oh, boy, it's good to see you.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.400
Well, you're some tonic for the old eyes yourself.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.360
Oh, how I missed you this summer.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.280
How long have you been here?

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.700
Oh, I've just been here a little while.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.620
Oh, boy, any good necking in sight for this year?

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.320
And why should this year be different?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.390
Ha, ha, ha.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.000
Hey, Frank, hop back.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:05.060
Hey, Eddie, what did you do all summer?

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.060
I've been selling acres.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.080
For boats?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.080
No, dumbbells, for floating kidneys.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.080
Golly, it's the same old room.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.430
Just as clean as a garage sink.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.630
Yes, but it's home sweet home to us.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:17.630
You betcha.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.630
Hey, you hillbilly.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.630
What's the matter?

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:23.140
Those dirty shoes.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.140
Dirty shoes?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.140
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.140
Hey!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.250
Ha!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.250
Ha!

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.460
Ha!

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:29.600
Ha!

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.810
- Comrade! Comrade! - Oh, boy!

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.790
- When did you get the swell rag? - Do you like it?

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:40.470
- Gee, that's a wow. - Well, it's yours, Biff.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.760
- Oh, no, Eddie, you keep it. - No, go on. I want you to have it.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.030
- Why, I bought it for you. - Oh, no, you didn't.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.980
- Sure. - Did you, Eddie?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.160
- Sure. - Gee, thanks.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.960
I thought it would look swell with those big banjo eyes.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.520
Yeah.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.000
And thanks very much for the present.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.370
- You know, I think you're sucking harder this year, Biff. - Yeah, I think so.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.520
Well, I hope you suck the line as hard.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.720
Well, if I do, I'll get another stripe this year.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.520
Yep, third and last one, huh?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.510
Gee, that's right. Only one more year.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.960
Gee, Biff, we've been roommates and teammates for three whole years.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.520
Three great years, old kid.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.760
You know, it kind of sucks the old heart when you realize

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:29.800
that a year from now, this will all be just a memory.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:38.120
There's something I wanted to tell you a hundred times, but every time I tried, why, the words sort of stuck.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.180
But I want you to know that our friendship has been the finest thing in my life.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.260
Oh, I don't say has been, Biff.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.720
This is always going to be until one of us kicks the last goal.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.840
Yes, and when he does, the other one will be right there backing up the line, won't he?

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.520
You betcha.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.790
Biff, you remember that first time we tangled?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.680
Almost split us up, didn't it?

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.000
When?

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.580
You know, freshman year.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.150
- What time I grabbed your blonde?

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.990
- You grabbed what blonde?

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.910
- Now, don't stall, you remember.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.410
- Why, you're as screwy as a kite.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.790
You couldn't take a femme from me,

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.030
blonde, brunette, red, gray, or bald.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.370
- I not only take 'em from you,

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.640
but I find you every honey you get.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.640
Why, if it weren't for me,

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.440
you'd be playing the old lady's home.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.280
- Yeah?

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.510
- And not doing so well, either.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.640
- Yeah?

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.900
- Well, you look at this layout.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.360
Now, show me one you ever gave me.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.060
Show me, you lop-eared chic.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.590
- What in that miserable collection of crocs?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.000
- Baloney, I'll show you some

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.440
It's real, honey.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.870
Hey, where's my trunk?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.070
- Where the heck's that trunk?

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.210
- Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.000
- Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.460
- Are you taking it on a sightseeing trip?

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.300
By the time you get up here,

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.230
all my clothes will be out of style.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.070
- But, sir--

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:44.860
- Shut up.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.640
To trunk or not to trunk, that is the question.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.480
- Yes, sir.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:53.400
- Yes, sir.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.050
- Make way for a senior.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.590
Out of my way, freshman, out of my way.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:07.570
You birds ought to be trained to carry trunks in your teeth and fly upstairs.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.210
Hey, freshman, where's my trunk?

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.740
Yes, sir, coming, sir, yes, sir.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.740
Hey, do you birds want to come up here perpendicular or horizontal?

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:17.740
Now snap into it.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:18.740
Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:23.220
Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.140
May an upperclassmen pass?

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:28.730
I said may an upperclassmen pass?

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.750
Yes, sir.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:30.000
Yes, sir.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:35.770
Snap it out. Move along.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.420
Hey, that's Eddie's trunk.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.120
You better keep playing around. Get that upstairs.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.860
Where the heck's my trunk?

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.750
Yes, they're coming, sir.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.150
For the love of Mike, where's that coming?

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.290
Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.630
Yes, sir, coming, sir.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:18.570
A peculiar form of exercise.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:19.590
Yes, sir.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:29.510
Say, no use trying to hide.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.480
Come out of there, come on, you freshmen.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.720
- Yes, sir.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:37.020
- Now listen, you birds have had it pretty soft today.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.640
But from now on, I wanna give you freshmen

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.420
a little advice for your own good.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.120
Keep up on your toes this time.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.410
- Yes, sir, yes, sir.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.370
- Park it over there.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:47.610
- Yes, sir, yes, sir.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.410
- Well, Biff, here we are, starting out the year

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.040
with the same old trouble with these microbes.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.100
Hey, up on your feet.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.440
- Yes, sir, yes, sir.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.240
- You freshmen remember that you are now

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.830
the scum of humanity.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.000
Sit down again in a senior's room and--

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.860
I absolutely guarantee to give you that school girl complexion you have heard so much about.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.020
Only not in the same place.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:07.700
Now beat it.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:08.610
Yes, sir.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.710
Hey, freshman, hold everything.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:11.150
Wait a minute.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.320
What is it, sir?

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.480
What is it, sir?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.540
No freshman has ever left this room alive without kissing the royal shoe.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.680
Why, what shoe, sir?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.580
What shoe, sir?

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.840
What shoe, mother, what shoe, mother?

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:26.030
This is Eddie's shoe of worldwide fame, the shoe that kicked the gold, that won the Stanford game.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.650
Now kiss it and make it big.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.370
Higher, sir.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.370
Open your toes, Cody.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:30.000
Take out the leg.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:36.460
- More passion! More cotton on half. - Let's hear it and make it big.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.080
- What idea? - My one idea, sir.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.840
- What idea, sir? - Having kissed the royal shoe with some clumsy efforts,

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.490
- what's the idea of hanging around? - Phone! Phone!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.530
That must be for me.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:59.860
Why?

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.560
it. I got it. Chi Sigma

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.300
house. Hello.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.810
Who?

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.250
Day.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.730
Such popularity. Must be

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.020
deserved. Oh, yes. It

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.200
is a lovely day.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:21.880
Who?

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.260
Will you describe him, please?

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.000
Oh, yes. I know

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.020
I don't know who you mean.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:36.080
Yes, I admit he has that school girl complex.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.080
What do you want?

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.960
Well, won't I do?

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.960
You know, I'm considered pretty good-looking myself.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.960
Yeah, behind your ears you are.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.040
Oh.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:52.040
Well, alright, if no one else will do, I'll get him.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.040
Who's working?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.360
Hey, handsome.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.340
Do your stuff.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.200
I might have known.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.000
Thank you.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.000
- That's what women want, that's me. - Yeah, ask her if her daughter's got a date for tonight.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:11.050
Listen, if you boys are going to act like this, I'll tell my girls not to call me up here anymore.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.050
And by the way, this is a private conversation.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:22.930
Oh, well, all right, all right. Since I'm going to speak English, none of you will understand a word of it anyhow.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:25.930
Hello, sweetheart.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.040
Speaking as Mo Levine. Pressing and cleaning.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:33.520
From last year I got a little bill from you.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.080
I'm sorry, but I'm all dated up for tonight.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:40.330
Sweetheart, I don't be fresher.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:44.050
By me, tailoring is a business, and ain't.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:47.730
Well, since you're so nice, I'll tell you what I'll do.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.180
Yes? Well?

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:53.330
I'll put your name on my waiting list, Bertie.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.970
Boy, I ain't.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.790
All right, don't do anything until you hear from me.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.010
Goodbye.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.000
Don't hang up, kid.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.560
Don't hang up.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.480
January 15th.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.760
Birdie.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:12.760
What is this strange power I have over women?

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.560
Maybe it's the way you have defense.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.980
I'll break that record.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.250
Can you give me Helen Gleeson's telephone number?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.220
Oxford 6254!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:48.880
Bevy, it looks as if the girls are starting in early this year to avoid the rush.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:53.710
Ooh, pretty. What is that, the Society for Lifted Faces?

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.270
Listen, kid, I'll show you some real honey.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.980
Say, Eddie, the team's got a tough schedule this year.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:00.870
Yeah, we sure have.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.810
I've decided we're going to cut out the women until after the football season's over.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.230
You?

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:06.610
Hey, are you serious?

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:07.650
I certainly am.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:09.390
All of them?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.040
Oh, not all of them.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:12.960
Every one of them.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:13.900
Ah, you're crazy.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:14.600
No, I mean it.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:16.440
Remember, this is our last year of football.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.280
Say, that's right.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:19.610
I hadn't thought about that.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.320
Last year of football?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.520
We got a whole lifetime of women.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:24.500
And how?

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.000
All right, boy, I'm with you.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:27.670
I'm off them till after the big game.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:28.730
That's great.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.000
Yes, sir, that's a good idea.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:43.570
Hey, Eddie, hey!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:56.510
I beg your pardon, were you looking for me?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.570
No, why?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.000
Well, most of the new girls

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.830
Oh, are you the Dean?

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:04.830
No, not exactly, but I know everything the Dean does,

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.830
and a whole lot he'd like to know.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:09.510
Then perhaps you can direct me to the English building.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.510
Which one?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.460
Are there two?

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:14.460
Oh, yes, there's that one that was cracked in the last earthquake.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.570
Oh, really?

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.570
That's the broken English building.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:21.300
I see. I suppose that's where you've been studying.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.220
I guess I want the other one.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.220
Well, now, let me see.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.220
No road map, no compass.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.270
Wait a minute, I've got an idea.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:30.000
Yes, I think I'll have time, too.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.760
- I can personally escort you. - Oh no, just direct me, please.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.670
Honey, when they're your size, I never direct them, I lead them.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:40.820
You couldn't find this place. It's two blocks over, three blocks around, knit two, purl two.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.410
You never could have found this place all by yourself.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:50.130
- Thank you. - Now, just a minute.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:53.950
You see, I have to make a little report of this to the Campus Welfare Society.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:57.130
- What did you say your name is? - I really didn't say.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:14:00.000
Well, you'll have to tell me. I'll get in trouble with the Society.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:04.300
- Hello, Baxter! - Oh, thanks!

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:08.090
I can't pronounce Baxter, so I'll just call you Bass.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.720
And the address, please?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.040
Oh, the Phi Phi house.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.670
Well, I'll be around tonight, about 8:00.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:22.560
- Am I supposed to first start cheering? - Not 'til after the first treatment.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.300
- I can hardly wait. - Don't be impatient.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.540
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:39.160
Oh, uh, pardon me, can you direct me to the campus candy store?

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:40.250
Huh?

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:43.650
Can you direct me to the campus candy store?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.660
You don't mean to tell me that an unprotected girl like yourself

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.440
is going to be seen going into the campus candy store in broad daylight.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:50.950
Why not?

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.180
Isn't so terrible?

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:52.860
Terrible?

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.930
Why, I alone have dragged from that opiate-wreaking atmosphere

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:57.730
the bodies of innocent young girls.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:00.000
Their sallow complexions, mute testimonies,

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:05.080
the lives they have led, sinful slaves to the chocolate broths, shameful addicts to the bonbons.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.580
You read that in a book someplace.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.520
Yeah, but it's pretty good, isn't it?

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:15.910
When I tell you what I can do, I can brave the terrorists at a campus candy store and bring you the candy myself.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:20.310
Oh, I would never forgive myself if anything happened to me.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:24.310
Oh, have no fear. Tonight, at the stroke of eight, I will arrive at...

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.150
Pie Pie House.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.540
And will there be welcome on the mat outside?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.810
Mm-hmm. And inside too.

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:36.270
Gee. This is my lucky day.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.310
Mine too.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:41.990
Well, uh...

